    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.move\n\n### Description\n\nUsing LSP to format the line is better than `=` because it takes into account everything to indent the line (code, Prettier, ESLint, etc..). Probably the performance of doing this is worst, but the dev experience will be better.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice if it is an optional configuration.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/25249581/e3fdf8d0-4e56-4d23-a9bf-4e5a9d2a266f\r\n\r\n",
